<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for March 26.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for March 26.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, on Tuesday published the following forecasts and data for gas consumption in the period March 24 to 26.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Mar 24 (actual) 254 mcm, 59 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 25 (forecast) 244 mcm, 57 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Mar 26 (forecast) 237 mcm, 55 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>Mar 24 (actual) 8.0 Celsius, seasonal normal 7.2 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 25 (forecast) 10.0 Celsius, seasonal normal 7.3 Celsius</p>
<p>Mar 26 (forecast) 11.1 Celsius, seasonal normal 7.4 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption on Tuesday, with none expected on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
